      "attrs": {
        "text": "You are fixing a flaky test in the Talium code-econ storage module. Work from `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ`. Canonical interpreter: **`venv/bin/python`** (has all deps).\n\n## The bug (confirmed by the controller)\n`src/server/storage/cli_schema_dump.py`'s `dump_ddl()` uses `create_mock_engine` + `Base.metadata.create_all(...)`, which emits each table's indexes in `table.indexes` **set iteration order** — nondeterministic across processes (depends on hash seed). The golden `tests/fixtures/storage_ddl.sql` captured one particular order (`uq_producers_key_hash` before `ix_producers_key_prefix`). Under the full test suite the order flips, so `tests/server/storage/test_schema_dump.py::test_ddl_matches_golden` FAILS intermittently (passes in isolation, fails whole-suite). Reproduce the failure: `venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` (whole repo) — you'll see 1 failed on `test_ddl_matches_golden`.\n\n## The fix\nMake `dump_ddl()` deterministic by emitting DDL explicitly with a stable index order instead of relying on `create_all`'s set order. Replace the body of `dump_ddl()` in `src/server/storage/cli_schema_dump.py` with an explicit compile approach:\n- Iterate `Base.metadata.sorted_tables` (already deterministic).\n- For each table: compile `sqlalchemy.schema.CreateTable(table)` against the postgresql dialect (`from sqlalchemy.dialects import postgresql; dialect = postgresql.dialect()`), then for each index in `sorted(table.indexes, key=lambda ix: ix.name)` compile `sqlalchemy.schema.CreateIndex(index)`.\n- Join statements the same way as before: each statement stripped + `\";\"`, joined by `\"\\n\\n\"`, trailing newline. Keep the output shape (a `;`-terminated statement per DDL, blank line between) so it stays a readable .sql file.\nLeave `main()` and the lazy `--er` import UNCHANGED.\n\nThen REGENERATE the golden: `PYTHONPATH=src venv/bin/python -m server.storage.cli_schema_dump --ddl > tests/fixtures/storage_ddl.sql`. Confirm it still contains all four `CREATE TABLE` blocks, both `GENERATED ALWAYS AS (...) STORED` columns on producers, and both producers indexes.\n\n## Prove determinism\nRun the whole-repo suite THREE times with different hash seeds and confirm the golden test passes every time:\n`for s in 0 1 2; do PYTHONHASHSEED=$s venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/server/storage/test_schema_dump.py -q; done`\nAll three must pass. Also run the full suite once: `venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` — expect green (0 failed; some skips are fine).\n\n## Commit\nCommit `src/server/storage/cli_schema_dump.py` and the regenerated `tests/fixtures/storage_ddl.sql` with message: `fix(storage): deterministic DDL dump (sorted indexes) to de-flake golden snapshot`.\n\n## Constraints\nNo \"Claude\" anywhere. Don't touch anything else.\n\n## Report\nAppend to `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-5-report.md` under \"## De-flake fix\": the change, the 3-seed determinism proof output, and the full-suite result. Reply with ONLY: Status, commit SHA + subject, the determinism/suite result (one line), report path.",
